    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Evaluate $1^2-2^2+3^2-4^2+\\cdots+99^2-100^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-5050$.\n\nPair consecutive squares to obtain $-(3+7+\\cdots+199)$.",
      "worked": "Let $S$ denote the given sum. Pair consecutive terms and use the difference of two squares.\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=(1-2)(1+2)+(3-4)(3+4)+\\cdots+(99-100)(99+100)\\\\S&=-(3+7+\\cdots+199)\\\\S&=-\\frac{50(3+199)}{2}\\\\S&=-5050.\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 50 terms in the arithmetic sequence $3,7,\\ldots,199$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
